---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Scholarship"
	description="Gavin Keulks — chapters and essays on the Amises, postmodernism and contemporary fiction, visual culture, and Aldous Huxley, plus the Martin Amis Web."
>
	<div class="wrap">
		<header class="page-head">
			<h1>Scholarship</h1>
			<p class="page-intro">
				Work for both general and specialized audiences.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="archive">
			<h2>The Martin Amis Web</h2>
			<p>
				I have overseen and administered{' '}
				<a href="https://martinamisweb.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the Martin&nbsp;Amis Web</a> since
				2006 &mdash; the authoritative digital archive for the author. The British
				Library designated it a site of scholarly significance in 2012 and
				archives it every six months as part of their ongoing UK Web Archive
				project. I built the site in 2006 and overhauled it in 2026.
			</p>
			<p>
				I have designed and maintained three other sites in the same period: the
				Western Oregon University Honors Program (2008&ndash;2026), the Faculty
				Senate (2010&ndash;2012), and the English Department (2007&ndash;2009).
			</p>
			<p>
				Administering an author archive has been a subject of my research as well
				as a task &mdash; on authorship, online archives, and intellectual property
				law.
			</p>
			<ul class="cite-list">
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Authorship in the Age of Digital Archiving.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					Technology, Knowledge, and Society International Conference.
					Toronto,&nbsp;Canada, 2017.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Authorship in the Age of Online Archiving.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					Popular and American Culture Association. Washington,&nbsp;DC, 2013.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Shadowy Margins and Sinkholes: Authorship, Online Archives, and
						IP&nbsp;Law.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					Popular and American Culture Association. Boston,&nbsp;MA, 2012.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;The Rhetoric of Road-Rage: Authorial Websites and Legal
						Hit-and-Runs.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					Popular and American Culture Association. San&nbsp;Antonio,&nbsp;TX, 2011.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Intellectual Properties: Growth Boundaries in Digital
						Scholarship and Copyright Law.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					Southwest/Texas Popular Culture Association. Albuquerque,&nbsp;NM, 2008.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Digital Humanizing: Administering Author/Scholar
						Relationships.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					Society for Digital Humanities. Saskatoon,&nbsp;Canada, 2007.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Administering Author Websites: Evolving Challenges in
						Scholarship, Copyright, and Discussion.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					Popular and American Culture Association. Boston,&nbsp;MA, 2007.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="work">
			<h2>The Amises</h2>
			<ul class="cite-list">
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Staging Amis: Autobiography and Autofiction.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
